'''Gerritsen Beach''' is a neighborhood in the [[New York City]] [[borough (New York City)|borough]] of [[Brooklyn]], located between [[Sheepshead Bay, Brooklyn|Sheepshead Bay]] to the west and [[Marine Park, Brooklyn|Marine Park]] to the east.<ref name="jmooneynyt">[https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/realestate/gerritsen-beach-brooklyn-living-in-the-art-of-hiding-in-plain-sight.html?pagewanted=all Mooney, Jake. "The Art of Hiding in Plain Sight," ''The New York Times'', Sunday, August 19, 2012.]</ref>  The area is served by [[Brooklyn Community Board 15]].<ref>[http://www.nyc.gov/html/cau/html/cb/cb_brooklyn.shtml Brooklyn Community Boards] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071221003420/http://www.nyc.gov/html/cau/html/cb/cb_brooklyn.shtml |date=2007-12-21 }}, [[New York City]]. express bus. Accessed December 31, 2007.</ref> The population of the neighborhood is 4,797 as of the 2020 U.S. census.
